flutter_edge_ai (patch_c_api.sh section 33): text LoRA sessions, a backport of
LiteRT-LM PR #2508 (leehack, "Support text LoRA sessions through
ResourceManager", head f51fe329, Apache-2.0) onto v0.20.0.

At v0.20.0 (and on main be6ce453) ResourceManager::CreateContextHandler builds
the ModelAssets of a not yet loaded text LoRA and then returns
InvalidArgumentError("Lora is not supported."); the LLM executor has no
LoadLoRA/UseLoRA and binds no LoRA buffers, although the scaffolding is there
(LoraManager, lora_id in the context, AssignLoraIdLocked).

From #2508: LoadLoRA/UseLoRA on LlmExecutorBase, implemented on the
compiled-model executor through LoraManager; forwarding in LockedLlmExecutor;
the context's lora_id kept through CloneContext and re-selected by
RestoreContext; SessionConfig keeps the LoRA paths; ResourceManager loads a
text LoRA once per id. Rebased onto v0.20.0's ResourceManager (scoped-file
keys, lora_mutex_ before executor_mutex_), mirroring its audio branch.

Not in #2508, added here: the LoRA inputs of every signature are bound, prefill
as well as decode (LoRA::GetLoRABuffers(signature), new in v0.20.0); a session
without an adapter on a model with LoRA inputs binds a LoRA whose every
tensor is zero, sized from the model's own LoRA inputs (the base weights;
LoRA::Create refuses data that matches no input, so an empty one cannot do); an active LoRA on a signature without LoRA inputs is an error
instead of being ignored. The NPU executor keeps the base LoadLoRA, which
returns Unimplemented. #2508's ResourceManager tests are not ported yet.

